WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.620
Marcus wants to pay a large premium into a cash-value life

2
00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:07.980
policy. The funding pattern can affect whether it becomes a modified

3
00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.480
endowment contract, usually called a MEC.

4
00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.060
A MEC still meets the federal definition of life insurance, but

5
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:19.520
it fails the applicable seven-pay funding test or comes from an

6
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.220
exchange of another MEC.

7
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.600
Its living distributions receive different tax treatment.

8
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:30.320
MEC status does not, by itself, remove the ordinary income-tax exclusion

9
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.080
for a qualifying death benefit.

10
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:37.380
Nor does it automatically require annual tax on all inside growth.

11
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:42.700
Identify the transaction: paying a premium, receiving a withdrawal,

12
00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.880
taking a loan or receiving a death payment.

13
00:00:46.794 --> 00:00:50.654
The seven-pay test compares premiums paid with the cumulative amount allowed

14
00:00:50.654 --> 00:00:52.474
at each point during the testing period.

15
00:00:53.094 --> 00:00:56.134
It is based on the actuarially determined premiums for paid-up future

16
00:00:56.134 --> 00:00:58.154
benefits after seven level annual payments.

17
00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:01.754
It is not simply the premium Marcus prefers or one-seventh of

18
00:01:01.754 --> 00:01:05.134
the death benefit. Suppose the facts give a ten thousand dollar

19
00:01:05.134 --> 00:01:09.134
seven-pay annual limit and a twenty thousand dollar
cumulative limit at the end of year two.

21
00:01:09.674 --> 00:01:13.094
Total counted premiums of twenty-two thousand dollars exceed that stated

22
00:01:13.094 --> 00:01:14.994
cumulative limit by two thousand dollars.

23
00:01:15.794 --> 00:01:19.514
Unless an applicable correction or other rule changes the facts, the

24
00:01:19.514 --> 00:01:23.514
funding test fails. Use the supplied limit rather than inventing an

25
00:01:23.514 --> 00:01:28.052
actuarial calculation. Passing the first seven years does not make every

26
00:01:28.052 --> 00:01:29.712
later policy change irrelevant.

27
00:01:30.552 --> 00:01:33.752
A material change can cause a new testing period with required

28
00:01:33.752 --> 00:01:38.552
adjustments. Certain benefit reductions can require recalculation using the

29
00:01:38.552 --> 00:01:43.932
lower benefit. Once MEC status applies, merely waiting until year eight

30
00:01:44.112 --> 00:01:47.612
or repaying a loan does not automatically remove it.

31
00:01:47.612 --> 00:01:52.252
A life policy received in exchange for a MEC is also

32
00:01:52.252 --> 00:01:55.212
a MEC under the exchange rule.

33
00:01:56.072 --> 00:02:00.232
The law provides specified procedures for timely return of excess premiums

34
00:02:00.232 --> 00:02:05.392
and other correction situations, but an ordinary withdrawal is not

35
00:02:05.392 --> 00:02:10.252
a universal cure. Ask the insurer to determine status and permitted

36
00:02:10.252 --> 00:02:14.772
correction before promising the tax result of a funding change.

37
00:02:15.582 --> 00:02:19.682
Compare two teaching policies, each with seventy thousand dollars of cash

38
00:02:19.682 --> 00:02:23.062
value and fifty thousand dollars of adjusted investment.

39
00:02:23.822 --> 00:02:26.502
Each therefore has twenty thousand dollars of gain.

40
00:02:27.422 --> 00:02:32.042
Assume an ordinary fifteen thousand dollar withdrawal from the non-MEC occurs

41
00:02:32.042 --> 00:02:36.182
after the first fifteen policy years, with no special rule or

42
00:02:36.182 --> 00:02:40.162
other adjustment. It is a basis recovery under those assumptions.

43
00:02:41.122 --> 00:02:43.682
Now apply the same withdrawal to the MEC.

44
00:02:44.342 --> 00:02:48.542
Its earnings-first rule makes the fifteen thousand dollars taxable ordinary

45
00:02:48.542 --> 00:02:51.742
income because twenty thousand dollars of gain is available.

46
00:02:52.622 --> 00:02:57.422
If the MEC withdrawal instead totals twenty-five thousand dollars, the first

47
00:02:57.422 --> 00:03:01.302
twenty thousand is gain and the remaining five thousand recovers basis.

48
00:03:02.376 --> 00:03:06.516
A MEC loan generally is treated as a distribution for federal

49
00:03:06.516 --> 00:03:11.476
tax purposes. Using the same seventy thousand dollar value and fifty

50
00:03:11.476 --> 00:03:16.036
thousand dollar adjusted investment, a fifteen thousand dollar loan is

51
00:03:16.036 --> 00:03:19.676
taxable to the extent of the available gain under the stated

52
00:03:19.676 --> 00:03:24.776
assumptions. Assigning or pledging value can also trigger distribution

53
00:03:24.776 --> 00:03:27.436
treatment, subject to specific exceptions.

54
00:03:28.256 --> 00:03:32.776
This differs from an ordinary loan under an in-force non-MEC policy.

55
00:03:33.636 --> 00:03:37.796
The tax classification does not eliminate the actual loan balance, interest

56
00:03:37.796 --> 00:03:39.936
or effect on insurance benefits.

57
00:03:40.896 --> 00:03:42.956
Keep those contract consequences separate.

58
00:03:43.956 --> 00:03:48.516
Also track prior taxable amounts so a later distribution calculation does

59
00:03:48.516 --> 00:03:50.496
not simply tax the same amount twice.

60
00:03:51.186 --> 00:03:55.919
Assume Marcus is forty-five and receives a MEC distribution with fifteen

61
00:03:55.919 --> 00:03:59.566
thousand dollars of taxable gain, with no applicable exception.

62
00:04:00.546 --> 00:04:03.806
The additional federal tax is ten percent of that taxable amount,

63
00:04:04.006 --> 00:04:07.986
or fifteen hundred dollars, on top of the ordinary income tax.

64
00:04:08.486 --> 00:04:10.806
It is not ten percent of the entire policy value.

65
00:04:11.526 --> 00:04:15.586
The additional-tax rule has exceptions, including distributions at age

66
00:04:15.586 --> 00:04:20.086
fifty-nine and one-half or later, qualifying disability and qualifying

67
00:04:20.086 --> 00:04:22.526
substantially equal periodic payments.

68
00:04:23.346 --> 00:04:26.926
An exception to the additional tax does not automatically remove ordinary

69
00:04:26.926 --> 00:04:28.586
income tax on the gain.

70
00:04:29.546 --> 00:04:34.026
On an exam, establish MEC status, calculate the gain portion,

71
00:04:34.946 --> 00:04:39.006
then check age and the actual exception
before calculating the extra tax.
